        ['Dona Timani', 'دونا تيماني', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '1'],
        ['Donna Khalife', 'دونا خليفة', '<div>Donna Khalifé is a singer, double bass player, composer, arranger&nbsp; born in Lebanon.&nbsp; &nbsp; She starts her first piano lessons at an early age. In 2003, she moves to Paris to continue her music studies: piano, orchestration, harmony … Her conducting classes with Nicolas Brochot and her jazz and improvisation classes with Guillaume Roy contribute a lot in shaping her musical sensibilities. Under Roy\'s guidance, she perfects her jazz singing, composing, arranging and improvisation, as well as her piano and double bass playing .&nbsp; &nbsp; As part of her education, she receives a 1st prize in orchestration at the Conservatoire Regional de Paris, a diploma in harmony and counterpoint, and she graduates in Jazz from the Conservatoire d\'Evry.&nbsp; &nbsp; Her eclecticism leads her to take part in different projects today, in Europe and Lebanon both as leader and side woman.&nbsp; &nbsp; She released her first album “ Heavy Dance” featuring her quintet, in March 2017 and is currently working on her second \"Hope is the thing with feathers\" to be out in 2019.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '                                                                                                                                        ', '1'],
        ['Association AFRIKAYNA', 'جمعية أفركاينا ', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '155'],
        ['ebrahim abdelmwala', 'ابزاهيم محمد محمود عبد المولي', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '71'],
        ['Echos Electrik', 'ايكو الكتريك', '<div>Echos Electrik is an association whose purpose is the development of digital cultures in Tunisia and more widely in Africa, through artistic expression and the cross-fertilization of North / South skills. She is at the origin of the creation in Tunisia of the E-FEST project, dedicated to the digital arts, which is now in its 12th edition, and produced a new decentralized initiative called No Logo, project of artistic and cultural promotion in the territories for the benefit of audiences remote from cultural institutions. Since its creation in 2007 in Paris and in 2012 in Tunis, Echos Electrik has developed important cultural and social initiatives devoted to new forms of artistic expression in connection with new technologies in all their diversity.&nbsp; &nbsp; More specifically, our mission is to anchor and reinforce innovative artistic practices, paying particular attention to the singularity of Languages ​​offered by the digital arts to be a present experience in Tunisia, giving each spectator and community of artists the opportunity to discover contemporary hybrid creations and to understand their modes of production.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '                                                                                                                                        ', '82'],
