        ['Health and Culture Center ', 'المركز الصحي الثقافي', '', '', '252'],
        ['Heba Khalifa', 'هبة خليفة', '<div>Heba Khalifa is a multimedia artist, photojournalist and painter. After graduating from the Faculty of Fine Arts in Cairo in 2000 with a bachelor’s degree in set design, she studied at the High Institute of Art Criticism. She started using photography as an essential part of her artistic projects and developed an interest in documenting and representing women and gender issues. Heba is also a founding member of the Shouf photographers collective.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '<div>هبة خليفة فنانة متعدّدة الوسائط ومصوّرة صحفية ورسامة. بعد تخرجها من كلية الفنون الجميلة في القاهرة عام 2000 وحصولها على بكالوريوس في تصميم ديكور المسرح، درست في المعهد العالي للنقد الفني. بدأت في استخدام التصوير الفوتوغرافي كجزء أساسي من مشاريعها الفنية وطوّرت اهتمامها بتوثيق وتمثيل قضايا النساء والجندر. هبة خليفة هي أيضاً عضوة مؤسّسة في مجموعة \"شوف\" للمصورين الفوتوغرافيين.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '71'],
        ['Heba Khamis', 'هبة محمد عبدالمنعم خميس', '<div>Heba Khamis an Egyptian photographer. won the first prize for world press photo 2018 award, Contemporary Issues stories. In 2017 she was selected for the Joop Swart masterclass from World Press Photo, Khamis got awarded with PHmuseum women photographers grant and the Ian Parry award. among other international awards.&nbsp; &nbsp; After graduating with a bachelor in painting, Heba did a career shift and worked as a photojournalist. Covered the two revolutions in Egypt and the aftermath. Later her photography developed from ha a more documentary style after volunteering in Uganda. Khamis became more focused on the social and humanitarian issues. She is working on mixing her artistic skills and the photojournalistic experience to have her own style in documentation.&nbsp; &nbsp; Recently she is working on breast ironing issue in Cameroon, Refugees gay prostitution in Germany, Transgenders in Egypt.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '                                                                                                                                        ', '71'],
        ['HEK-MA', 'حكمة', '', '', '82'],
        ['Hela Belhadj Ali', 'هالة بالحاج علي', '                                    <div>Hela Belhadj is a Tunisian singer and songwriter, passionate about music from childhood, she started singing and playing keyboard when she was 10 years old than learning to play violin in her preparatory school music club, she joined the conservatory a couple of years later trying to know more about music world and refine her singing and violin playing.    At 2005, she formed her first music band \"heaven\'s Rose\" interpreting covers for world, pop and rock music and some originals, then later a second one \"caravan\", she was performing alone meanwhile and got awarded for some of her compositions till she finally felt ready to start building a solo career where she can express her ideas and art independently and work more on her own music and songs.    The diversity of music she was influenced by is reflecting the divergence of her compositions.With lyrics written in Arabic (Tunisian dialect) the most but also in English and French, she hopes to deliver messages and feelings to more people around the world.    The last two years was dedicated to the production of her first music album: “Tasswera” . With the support of Arab Fund for Arts and Culture, she was finally able to record six songs of her lyrics and melodies varying from pop to flamenco to oriental music, the songs brings together nostalgia for yesterday, rebellion on today\'s reality, and an invitation for change and hope for a better tomorrow. The album will be soon released to the audience through Social Media with videos that are currently in the making.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                    ', '                                                                                                                                        ', '233'],
        ['Héla Ben Bhecher', 'هالة بن بشر', '', '', '233'],
        ['HelaHelp National Organization', 'منظمة هيلا هيلب الوطنية', '', '', '216'],
        ['Hesham Abed', 'هشام عابد', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '71'],
        ['Hesham Elsherif', 'هشام الشريف', '<div>Hesham Elsherif, born in 1997, is an independent photographer based in Egypt. He started photography in 2013 by documenting the civil unrest Egypt witnessed after the Egyptian army ousted Mohammed Morsi, Egypt’s first freely elected president. At the time, he was a 16-year-old student with a point-and-shoot camera, living in a village located 100-kilometers southwest of the capital, Cairo. Since then, he became interested in documenting the daily life of his hometown, Fayoum, as well as covering in-depth cultural and social documentary stories.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '                                                                                                                                        ', '71'],
        ['Hewar company for independent theater and performing arts', 'حوار للمسرح المستقل والفنون الآدائية', '<div>Hewar is an independent theater and performing arts company based in Alexandria, Egypt. Hewar works on three main threads: 1) the Theater Is A Must International Independent Theater Festival in Alexandria, 2) capacity building and training projects for independent emerging artists and theater and performing arts practitioners, and 3) staging theater productions focused on cross-cultural collaborations concerned with local and global political contexts presented in post-dramatic and political dramaturgy-based productions.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '<div>\"حوار للمسرح المستقل والفنون الأدائية\" شركة مسرح وفنون آداء مستقلة مقرها الإسكندرية، مصر. تعمل شركة حوار على ثلاثة محاور رئيسية: مهرجان وملتقى \"لازم مسرح\" وهو مهرجان دولي مستقل للمسرح وفنون الأداء في الإسكندرية، والمشاريع التدريبية وبناء القدرات للفنانين والفنانات الشباب في مجال المسرح المستقل وفنون الأداء، والإنتاج المسرحي الذي يركز على التعاون الدولي بين الثقافات ويهتم بشكل أساسي بالسياقات السياسية المحلية والعالمية التي تتجلى من خلال الإنتاجات المسرحية ما بعد الدرامية والسياسية.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '71'],
        ['Hiba Alansari', 'هبة الأنصاري', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '222'],
        ['Hiba Mehrez', 'هبه محرز', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '222'],
        ['Hicham  Gardaf', 'هشام غرداف', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '155'],
        ['Hicham Bouzid', 'هشام بوزيد', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '155'],
        ['Hilal Chouman', 'هلال شومان', '                                    <div><div>Hilal Chouman is a novelist born in Beirut in 1982. He currently resides in Canada. He has published five novels in Arabic. His latest is titled <i>Sorrow in My Heart</i>. An English translation of his novel <i>Limbo Beirut</i> was included in the Saif Ghobash–Banipal Prize shortlist and the Pen Translation Award longlist.</div></div>                                                                                                    ', '                                    <div>هلال شومان روائي لبناني الجنسية، وُلِد في بيروت في العام 1982. نًشِرَ له بالعربيّة حتى الآن أربع روايات: \"ما رواه النوم\" (دار ملامح - 2008)، و\"نابوليتانا\" (دارالآداب - 2010)، \"ليمبو بيروت\" (دار التنوير - 2012)، و\"كانَ غدًا\" (دار الساقي - ٢٠١٦). يتابع نشر المقالات النقدية والنصوص الأدبية بشكل غير دوري في مواقع وصحف لبنانية وعربية. يقيم حاليًا في دبي بالإمارات العربية المتحدة.    موقعه على الإنترنت: http://www.hilalchouman.com</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                    ', '1'],
        ['Hind Oudrhiri', 'هند الودغيري', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '155'],
        ['Hisham Jaber ', 'هشام جابر', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '1'],
        ['Hisham Naddaf ', 'هشام نداف ', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '222'],
        ['Hoda Barakat', 'هدى بركات', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '1'],
        ['Hoda Omran', 'هدى عمران', '<div>Hoda Omran is a poet, novelist, editor and researcher. She studied political science at Cairo University and is completing a master’s thesis on cultural policies and feminist literature. Her published works include the poetry collection <i>Naive and Sentimental</i> (2016), with selected poems translated into Swedish and English; the novel <i>Fish, Orange, Weed</i> (Dar Al-Saqi, 2018), which received a grant from the Arab Fund for Arts and Culture (AFAC) and was shortlisted for the Sawiris Award in 2021; and the poetry collection <i>Cairo</i> (2022), General Egyptian Book Organization, poetry series), winner of the Helmy Salem Prize for Poetry. She has also published the poetry collection <i>As If It Were Forgiveness</i> (Safsafa, 2023) and the short story collection <i>Violent Love</i> (Kotob Khan, 2024). Her young adult novel project <i>The Gamer’s Life</i> received a Mophradat Writing Sabbaticals grant in 2021. Hoda has also worked as an editor at Kotob Khan publishing house.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '<div>شاعرة وروائية ومحررة وباحثة. درست العلوم السياسية في جامعة القاهرة، وتعمل على إنهاء رسالة الماجستير عن السياسات الثقافية والأدب النسوي. نشر لها: ديوان شعر \"ساذج وسنتمنتالي\" (2016)، الذي ترجمت بعض قصائده للغتين السويدية والإنجليزية، ورواية \"حشيش سمك برتقال\" عن دار الساقي 2018، والتي حصلت على منحة من صندوق الثقافة العربي – آفاق، ووصلت إلى القائمة القصيرة في جائزة ساويرس لعام 2021، وديوان \"القاهرة\" (2022) عن الهيئة العامة للكتاب ضمن سلسلة الشعر، والذي فاز بجائزة حلمي سالم للشعر. صدر لها أيضاً مجموعة قصصية بعنوان \"حب عنيف\" عن دار نشر الكتب خان 2024، وديوان شعر \"كأنها مغفرة\" عن دار نشر صفصافة 2023. حاز مشروع رواية \"حياة الجيمرز\"، وهي رواية للمراهقين، على منحة مؤسسة مفردات للتفرغ لعام 2021. عملت كمحررة لدار نشر الكتب خان.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '71'],
