        ['Wessal Mahmoud', 'وصال محمود', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '71'],
        ['Wessam Talhouq', 'وسام تلحوق', '<div>Wessam Talhouq, actor, theatre Director, and trainer.1983, Damascus-Syria. Living and working in Germany since 2015. He worked in diverse artistic and cultural projects in Hannover, Berlin, and Göttingen where he directed his last theater play \"Nora and her other name\", 2018.&nbsp; &nbsp; Wessam graduated from the \"Higher Institute of dramatic arts\", Damascus, Syria, 2010; Where he worked as a teacher assistant, 2013-2014. He worked as a theater trainer in The interactive theater project in public schools, in Syria, 2011-2012. Wessam also worked as a director and actor in several theater plays and performances in MENA region &amp; Europe.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '<div>وسام تلحوق ممثل ومخرج مسرحي، من مواليد دمشق 1983. يعيش ويعمل في ألمانيا منذ 2015 حيث أدار العديد من ورش العمل كمدرب مسرح. كما عمل في العديد من العروض المسرحية، كان آخرها إخراج العرض المسرحي \"نورا واسمها الأخر\" في مدينة غوتنغن، 2018.&nbsp; &nbsp;تخرج وسام من&nbsp; قسم التمثيل في المعهد العالي للفنون المسرحية في دمشق، 2010. عمل في ما بعد في نفس القسم أستاذاً مساعداً في مادتي فن التمثيل والمختبر المسرحي، 2013-2014. كما كان منشطاً ومدرباً مسرحياً ضمن مشروع المسرح التفاعلي في المدارس الحكومية في دمشق، 2011-2012. لقد شارك في السابق كممثل ومخرج في أعمال مسرحية في بعض دول حوض المتوسط&nbsp; وأوروبا.&nbsp;&nbsp;</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '222'],
        ['Wiame Haddad', 'وئام الحداد', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '233'],
        ['Wissam Arbache', 'وسام عربش', '', '', '82'],
        ['Wissam Murad', 'وسام مراد', '', '', '175'],
        ['Witte de With Center for Contemporary Art', 'مركز فيته دي فيت للفن المعاصر', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '161'],
        ['Yaa Samar! Dance Theatre', 'فرقة يا سمر! للمسرح الراقص', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '175'],
        ['Yacine Boulares', 'ياسين بولاعراس', '<div>Tunisian saxophonist, clarinetist and composer based in Brooklyn, NY .A graduate from La Sorbonne in Philosophy and the Conservatoire National de Paris, he is also a Fulbright and New School for Jazz grantee.&nbsp; A versatile musician and composer, his debut album AJOYO was released in 2015 on Ropeadope Records and played on radios throughout the world from New Yorks\' WNYC to French RFI, London\'s Jazz FM, National radio in Brazil… A sought after sideman and arranger, he regularly records and performs with the likes of Placido Domingo (Encanto Del Mar), Tabou Combo, Sheila Jordan... In 2015 his project Abu Sadiya with Vincent Segal and Nasheet Waits is awarded the French American Jazz Exchange and the AFAC grant. The trio album, exploring the Tunisian Stambeli, was released in 2017 on the French label Accords Croisés and premiered in the US at the Lincoln Center Atrium in April 2018. Acclaimed by the press after its French release the trio was programmed at the Jazzahead festival in Bremen, Germany.&nbsp; Yacine Boulares is also involved in many creative projects with schools and community-based organizations in the US. In 2016-17 he is an artist in residence at the Baltimore School for the arts where he is commissioned to compose a suite of songs blending Jazz with West and North African rhythms. Yacine is a D\'Addario woodwinds and Lebayle Mouthpieces artist.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                                                        ', '                                                                                                                                        ', '233'],
        ['Yalda Younes', 'يلدا يونس', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '1'],
        ['Yamen Mohamad', ' يامن محمد', '', '', '222'],
        ['YANTE – Youth, Art, and Levante', 'يانته - يوث٬ ارت٬ اند ليفانته', '', '', '175'],
        ['Yasir El Tigani', 'ياسر التيجاني', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '216'],
        ['Yasser Abdelhafez', 'ياسر عبد الحافظ', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '71'],
        ['Yasser Abdo Ahmad', 'ياسر عبده أحمد', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '252'],
        ['Yasser Sha\'ban', 'ياسر شعبان', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '71'],
        ['Yassine Abou El-Haytham', 'ياسين أبو الهيتم', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '155'],
        ['Yassine Balbzioui', 'ياسين بالبزيوي', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '155'],
        ['Yazan Al-Hajari', 'يزن الهجري', 'Yazan is a songwriter and composer from Syria now living near New York City. He wrote his first song on the piano when he was nine years old and has continued to write songs and develop himself as an artist since. His music will often integrate styles from Arabic, jazz, folk and classical music. Yazan released his first album, Fi mazih, Fi jad, in 2010 then performed in Beirut with his theatrical band Hat Lan Shouf. He composed songs for many Arab singers like Hiba Tawaji, Macadi Nahhas, Basma Jabr, and made music for Media and video arts. He recorded his second album, Prophet of Glass, in 2018, in the U.S., where he studied jazz performance. His work aims to explore ideas like identity, East and West, home and exile, by using different cultural backgrounds and practices and blending various categories, concepts, sounds, poetry and visual art.', '                                                                    ', '222'],
        ['Yazan Alkhalili', 'يزن الخليلي', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '121'],
        ['Yazan Kopty', 'يزن قبطي', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '175'],
        ['Yazid Anani', 'يزيد عناني', '                                    <div>Yazid Anani was born in 1975, Ramallah. He is an assistant professor at the Department of Architecture and the Master Program in Urban Planning and Landscape – Birzeit University, Palestine. Yazid Anani chaired the Academic Council of the International Art Academy Palestine 2010 – 2012. He is part of several collectives, and projects such as Decolonizing Architecture and Ramallah Syndrome and has curated and co-curated several projects such as Urban Cafés, Palestinian Cities – Visual Contention and the 2nd, 3rd and 4th editions of Cities Exhibition and took part in several art projects. Anani has lectured and published internationally on issues of architecture and urban transformations, colonial spaces and power relations, public art and public spaces and art education. He is also the director of Public Program at the A.M. Qattan Foundation in Ramallah.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                    ', '                                    <div>يزيد عناني (١٩٧٥) رام الله. عمل كأستاذ مساعد في دائرة الهندسة المعمارية وبرنامج الماجستير في التخطيط الحضري في جامعة بيرزيت، ٢٠٠٧ - ٢٠١٦، فلسطين. ترأس المجلس الأكاديمي في الأكاديمية الدولية للفنون فلسطين ٢٠١٠ - ٢٠١٢. وهو جزء من العديد من، المجموعات الفنية مثل متلازمة رام الله (Ramallah Syndrome) وتفكيك عمارة الاحتلال (Decolonizing Architecture). وقد قام كقيم بالمشاركة وتنظيم العديد من المشاريع الفنية ومنها المقاهي الحضرية، والمدن الفلسطينية – إشكاليات بصرية والنسخ الثانية والثالثة والرابعة والخامسة والسادسة من معرض المدن – متحف جامعة بيرزيت وخارج الأرشيف – بلدية رام الله وأمم متعاقدة من الباطن – مؤسسة عبد المحسن القطان. يحاضر عناني وينشر محليا وعالميا في قضايا العمارة والتحولات الحضرية، والفضاءات الاستعمارية وعلاقات القوة، وتدخلات الفن في الفضاءات العامة والتعليم الفني. ويعمل حاليا مديرا للبرنامج العام في مؤسسة عبد المحسن القطان في رام الله.</div><div><br></div>                                                                                                    ', '175'],
        ['Ymane Fakhir', 'إيمان فخير', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '155'],
        ['Younes Baba-Ali', 'يونس بابا علي', '                                                                    ', '                                                                    ', '155'],
